.TH "ET\-INDEX" "1" "November 2026" ""
.SH NAME
et\-index \- list and rebuild EmComm Tools offline indices
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]et\-index\f[R] \f[B]list\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]et\-index\f[R] \f[B]reindex\f[R] \f[I]INDEX\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]et\-index\f[R] manages offline indices used by the EmComm Tools
API.
.PP
Use \f[B]list\f[R] to display available indices or \f[B]reindex\f[R] to
rebuild a specific index.
Only indices with an existing directory can be selected.
.PP
Reindexing stops the EmComm Tools API user service, removes the selected
index directory, and restarts the service.
.PP
The EmComm Tools API automatically rebuilds missing indices when it
starts.
The \f[B]et\-index\f[R] command does not perform the rebuild itself.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\f[B]list\f[R]
List the available indices, one per line.
.TP
\f[B]reindex\f[R] \f[I]INDEX\f[R]
Remove the specified index and restart the EmComm Tools API service.
The API automatically rebuilds the missing index during startup.
The index must be available in the \f[B]list\f[R] output.
.SH AVAILABLE INDICES
.TP
\f[B]faa\f[R]
FAA index.
.TP
\f[B]license\f[R]
License index.
.TP
\f[B]zip2geo\f[R]
ZIP\-to\-geolocation index.
.PP
Only indices whose directories exist are shown by \f[B]list\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
List available indices:
.IP
.EX
et\-index list
.EE
.PP
Rebuild the license index:
.IP
.EX
et\-index reindex license
.EE
.SH WHEN TO RUN
Run \f[B]et\-index\f[R] when an offline index needs to be rebuilt.
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[B]/opt/emcomm\-tools\-api/index/\f[R]
Directory containing the offline indices.
Reindexing deletes the selected index subdirectory before restarting the
API service.
